Z||000012||Steve Normington||07-20-2001||04:31 PM||||Why not get a wheel trailer (not sure of name)? By that I mean the trailer where only one set of wheels go on the trailer and the other set ride on the pavement.<P>I think the RV you are describing is called a toy trailer.||||reg||1
Z||000013||CoolBlue87GT||07-20-2001||07:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR>[B]Why not get a trailer where only one set of wheels go on the trailer and the other set ride on the pavement.<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's called a dolly.  I'd rather have all wheels off the ground.  Just my preference. Less chance of getting damaged.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000014||CoolBlue87GT||07-20-2001||08:15 PM||||Here is a few Pic of one trailer for sale locally.  The guy used it for hauling furniture a few times (that's his story)<P>It's in fair shape, needs 4 new tires. Has brakes on the rear axle only.  Told me he had a blow out on the left the last trip, and on the return trip the right side blew !<P>Both were on the rear. - Wonder if it had somthing to do with the brakes.<P>I'd need to build ramps, theres a spot where they would hook in.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1_89.jpg"> <BR>He's asking in the paper 1250<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1_94.jpg">  <BR>After talking, he offered 1100<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1_98.jpg">  <BR>I'm thinking more like 800<P><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000015||hugh||07-20-2001||08:51 PM||||Even if you do get it for $800,how much will you have to spend on it to make it good enough and safe enough to use?Now how far away from the price of a new trailer are you?Is it worth it?You could  actually spend more to make it right than it would cost to buy new.I'm speaking from experience,not with a trailer,but with a car that was free.I lost money and gave it away just to get rid of it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||CoolBlue87GT||07-20-2001||09:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Even if you do get it for $800,..Now how far away from the price of a new trailer are you?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, you are correct. I've been looking at that.  The one company I have putting together plans for me estimate the price at 1900 - 2000 range.<P>That's everything with brakes on all 4 wheels, 15' trailer tires, 2 x 6 wood floor dove tailed in the rear w/ ramps.<P>I'd need to add Electric brake controller in the Cherokee, about 150, get an equalizer hitch w/ sway bar - that's about 300 or so.<P>I want to do it right, and safe.||||reg||1
Z||000017||skitime||07-20-2001||10:07 PM||||You need it enclosed. You need it enclosed. You need it enclosed. You need it enclosed.<BR>You need it enclosed. You need it enclosed.<BR>Did I mention that you need it enclosed? Don't you remember that rock nick on the way to Carlisle. Now if you get a nick on the way to a show and another nick on the way back you will have at least two nicks per show. You will have gone to three shows that I know of, so that is 6 nicks per year.  If you keep showing the car for ten years you will have 60 nicks. I would hate to see your car with 60 nicks. Wouldn't you? Just think if you go to even more shows!||||reg||1
